course: dictionary
lesson: 435
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word arch can be a curved shape, a part of your foot, or a verb meaning to bend into a curve. Read the words around it to decide.
explain: «Waves cut caves into headlands, the caves join into arches, and when arches fall, stacks are left.» Here arches are curved shapes made of rock by the sea. Ask yourself: what would fit in this sentence? A curved rock shape fits, but a foot does not.
explain: «A frightened cat arches its back.» This time arches is a verb. The cat bends its back into a curve. Test your meaning in the sentence: the cat bends its back into a curve, and it still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: An arch is a curved shape or structure, like the top of a doorway or a bridge.
fact: The arch of your foot is the curved part underneath, between your heel and your toes.
fact: To arch means to bend into a curved shape, like a cat arching its back.
fact: Arch- at the start of a word means chief or main, as in archenemy.
fact: Romans built strong stone arches for bridges and aqueducts.
exercise: «A beam bridge rests on supports, while an arch pushes the weight sideways and down into the ground.» In this sentence, what is an arch? | A kind of cat | A part of your foot | A loud noise | *A curved structure that carries weight
exercise: «A frightened cat arches its back, stands sideways and fluffs out its fur.» What does arches mean here? | Stretches out flat on the floor | Goes to sleep | *Bends into a curve | Jumps over the fence
exercise: «The arch of Mia's foot hurt after the long run.» What does arch mean here? | A bridge over a river | *The curved part under your foot | The top of a doorway | A loud shout
test: In «Roman stone arch bridges still stand after about 2,000 years», what is an arch? | A soft, wet hill | *A curved structure that goes up and over | A chief or main person | A kind of fish
test: Sam reads about his archenemy in a story. What does arch- mean at the start of a word? | *Chief or main | Very old | Curved | Wet and grey
exam: «A stiff body, raised hair, a growl, or an arched back on a cat all say «go away».» What does arched mean here? | Stretched out flat | Happy and relaxed | *Bent into a curve | Very quiet
